      "reasons": [
        "The packet specifies a DSM-5-based criterion for depressive disorder: “five (or more) of the following symptoms” present during the same 2-week period, with at least one symptom being depressed mood or loss of interest/pleasure. The definition omits this “five (or more)” requirement, making part of the diagnostic criteria unsupported/insufficiently specified.",
        "The packet’s descriptor is explicitly labeled “Depressive Disorder, Major” (DSM-5) while the definition uses the broader term “clinical depression” without tying it to “major” as in the packet, leaving the requested sense under-supported by the supplied source."
